  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of evidence-based emergency protection and health care assistance to the most vulnerable migrant workers and their families impacted by multipronged crises in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide emergency protection and health care to vulnerable migrant workers and their families impacted by the humanitarian crisis in Lebanon. Activities include collecting displacement data to inform humanitarian response in south Lebanon, ensuring healthcare to migrant workers and their families through dedicated &#x2018;health days&#x2019; initiatives, financially supporting the life and limb saving healthcare of migrants, and providing specialized assistance and awareness raising for migrant workers and their children in the form of child protection case management, psychosocial support, and cash for protection and legal assistance. Under the Health sector, this project will support 2,020 individuals, including 1,305 women, 145 children, and 8 persons with disabilities. Under the protection sector, this project will support 2,568 people including 2,055 women and 40 persons with disabilities. Under the Child Protection sector, this project will support 535 individuals, including 400 women and 5 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
